# Portfolio Website

A dark, blueprint-inspired single-page portfolio built with **plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript**: no frameworks, no build step. It combines a technical grid aesthetic with smooth scroll-driven animation and a custom cursor.

> **Live demo:** `<add your GitHub Pages / Netlify / Vercel link>`
> **Author:** Faizan Shafi

<!-- Add a screenshot or GIF here: ![Preview](assets/preview.png) -->

---

## Features

- **Animated loading screen** with a progress bar that fades out after the page loads
- **Custom cursor**: a lagging ring plus a precise dot, with an enlarged hover state on interactive elements
- **Scroll progress bar** fixed at the top of the viewport
- **Scroll-reveal animations** powered by `IntersectionObserver`
- **Animated stat counters** that count up when they enter the viewport
- **Side dot navigation** that highlights the current section and scrolls smoothly on click
- **Hero "blueprint" graphic**: concentric rotating rings, glowing nodes, and a mouse-driven parallax effect
- **Experience cards** and a **vertical roadmap timeline** with active/next states
- **Fully responsive** layout with breakpoints at 1024px, 768px and 480px, plus a full-screen mobile menu
- **Design tokens** defined as CSS custom properties for easy re-theming

## Tech Stack

| Area | Details |
| --- | --- |
| Markup | HTML5 |
| Styling | CSS3: custom properties, Grid, Flexbox, `clip-path`, `backdrop-filter`, keyframe animations |
| Behaviour | Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+), `IntersectionObserver`, `requestAnimationFrame` |
| Fonts | [Space Grotesk](https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Space+Grotesk), [Space Mono](https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Space+Mono), [Inter](https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Inter) via Google Fonts |

## Project Structure

Adjust the paths below to match your repository.

```
.
├── index.html
├── css/
│   └── style.css
├── js/
│   └── main.js
└── README.md
```

### Page sections

| Section | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| Hero | Headline, subtitle, call-to-action buttons, animated blueprint graphic |
| Stats | Four animated counters |
| About | Short bio and tech-stack tags |
| Experience | Cards with company, product, period and responsibilities |
| Roadmap | Timeline of milestones (`current`, `active`, `next` states) |
| Contact | Large heading and contact link |
| Footer | Credits and location line |

## Getting Started

No dependencies are required.

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/faizanshafi25/<your-repo>.git
cd <your-repo>

# 2. Open index.html in your browser
#    or serve it locally:
npx serve .
# or
python -m http.server 8000
```

Then visit `http://localhost:8000` (or the port shown).

## Customisation

### Theme

All colours live in `:root` at the top of the stylesheet:

```css
:root {
    --bg: #0a0a0f;
    --surface: #12121a;
    --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    --text: #e8e8ed;
    --text-secondary: #6b6b7b;
    --accent: #4f46e5;
    --accent-glow: rgba(79, 70, 229, 0.15);
    --cyan: #22d3ee;
    --grid-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
}
```

Change these values to re-theme the whole site.

### Content

- **Stats:** set the target number with `data-count` on the `.stat-number` element. The counter increments by one every 200 ms.
- **Experience:** duplicate an `.exp-card` and edit the company, product, period and list items.
- **Roadmap:** duplicate a `.roadmap-item`. Add `current` for the highlighted marker, and use `.status.active` or `.status.next` for the status label.
- **Loader duration:** the loader hides after 2200 ms; change the timeout in the `load` listener (and the `loaderFill` animation length in CSS to match).

### Required element hooks

The JavaScript looks up these elements, so keep them in your HTML:

| Selector | Used for |
| --- | --- |
| `#loader` | Loading screen |
| `#cursor`, `#cursorDot` | Custom cursor |
| `.hoverable` | Elements that trigger the cursor hover state |
| `#scrollProgress` | Scroll progress bar |
| `.scroll-reveal`, `.stat-item`, `.exp-card`, `.roadmap-item`, `.contact-heading`, `.contact-sub`, `.contact-link` | Scroll-reveal targets |
| `section[id]` and `.side-nav-dot[data-section]` | Side navigation (the `data-section` value must match a section `id`) |
| `#mobileBtn`, `#mobileMenu`, `.mobile-link` | Mobile menu |
| `.blueprint-container` | Hero parallax |

## Browser Support

Works in current versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari. It relies on `backdrop-filter`, `clip-path`, CSS `inset`, and `IntersectionObserver`.

## Known Limitations & Roadmap

- [ ] Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` by disabling heavy animations
- [ ] Show the native cursor on touch devices and when `prefers-reduced-motion` is set (the page currently uses `cursor: none` globally)
- [ ] Add keyboard focus styles for the side navigation dots and buttons
- [ ] Add `aria-label` attributes to the mobile menu button
- [ ] Self-host fonts to remove the Google Fonts dependency

## Deployment

The site is static, so it can be hosted anywhere:

- **GitHub Pages:** *Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch → `main` / root*
- **Netlify / Vercel:** import the repository; no build command needed, publish directory `/`

